Cooperative-learning engine vendored from the R package multiview (GPL-2).

Upstream authors:
  Daisy Yi Ding, Robert J. Tibshirani, Balasubramanian Narasimhan,
  Trevor Hastie, Kenneth Tay, James Yang, Jonathan Taylor

Source: CRAN multiview version 1.0 (2026-05-11)
https://cran.r-project.org/package=multiview
Upstream source tarball SHA-256:
91ba5b33170392a6298d4d1bb9b051df5ade412aa55ff7fe4ae2c89ff833f9d5

Imported files:
  R/cooperative-*.R (renamed from the upstream R sources),
  src/wls_exp.cpp, src/driver.h, and src/glmnetpp/.

Local modifications:
  upstream R symbols were given the cooperative- file prefix; calls were
  adapted to the stablr namespace and manual cooperative S3 registrations;
  a stablr-facing backend and validation/provenance layer were added; and the
  native registration/build files were integrated with stablr. Algorithmic
  cooperative-learning code remains derived from multiview 1.0.

This component is licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 2.
See https://www.gnu.org/licenses/old-licenses/gpl-2.0.html

When distributing stablr, the cooperative-learning sources in
R/cooperative-*.R and src/ (including glmnetpp headers) remain
under GPL-2. The package is distributed under GPL (>= 2) to provide one
consistent license for the combined work.
